  "commit": {
    "sha": "01c41e8ba2aad586ec885c92bc4b959a49005eda",
    "date": "2026-10-15T06:19:00Z",
    "message": "library: a skill probe's download goes when it is probed again or 15 minutes are up, and one a magpie that quit left behind goes at the next probe (#2321)\n\nProbeSkills kept each GitHub probe's download, a magpie-skill-* folder in\nthe temp dir, cached for 15 minutes. An expired one went only at the\n*next* probe, so a magpie that quit, or a test that ended, left it there\nfor good. One go test ./internal/library left 22. This machine's temp dir\nhad 5477, and with old test homes they filled the disk under a full run\n(gateway tests failed \"no space left on device\").\n\n- keepProbe: each cached probe has a timer that removes its folder when\n  probeLife is up. A probe of the same input replaces it and removes the\n  old folder at once, outside the lock.\n- sweepStaleDownloads, at each probe: a magpie-skill-* in the temp dir over\n  an hour old goes. No live one is that old, since a probe is kept 15\n  minutes and a fetch takes seconds.\n- internal/library's TestMain gives the tests a temp dir of their own\n  (TMPDIR, and TMP/TEMP for Windows), ends the cached probes, and fails a\n  run that leaves a skill download there. A test binary started again by a\n  test keeps its parent's temp dir.\n\nRun (on origin/main 8b89b2e36): go test -count=1 -timeout 60m ./... all ok;\ngofmt clean; go vet darwin, GOOS=linux -tags nogui, GOOS=windows clean.\n\nBroken by hand, each went red:\n- a replaced probe's folder kept (TestProbeDownloadEndsWithIt)\n- no removal at expiry (TestProbeDownloadEndsWithIt)\n- the sweep ignores age, or the prefix, or doesn't run\n  (TestStaleDownloadsSwept)\n- TestMain doesn't end the probes: \"the tests left 16 skill downloads\"\n\nNot tried: the Windows box, though TMP/TEMP are set for it."
  },
  "scope": "25 selected guideline, subsystem, workflow and verification documents; not a full code review"
